From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:15:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/18] nemotron: checkpoint prompt passes run the FP8 layers
 in 128-row tiles

ck.lane8 took its widest FP8 tile at 64 rows by 64 columns. Calls of 128 rows or more now take tf_ck8_128 (128 rows by
64 columns) or, where K slices meet in a cluster, tf_ck8_128c (128 by 128): eight warps in two rows of 64, up to
64 KiB of shared memory. Each row keeps its K slices, MMA steps and summation order, so its bits are the decode tiles'.
`tf-cuda-test checkpoint` compares 129-row calls with the same rows one at a time at three shapes.
